{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":1111,"final_message_hash":"sha256:ee9b6a698b9e44975ea03ca2d04cc5eeca643efa48113d31006ff8583049ffc4","final_message_inline":"The code was wrong, not the test.\n\n**Cause:** `hashKey` folds to a *signed* 32-bit int (`h | 0`), so roughly half of all keys hash negative. `shardFor` used plain `hashKey(key) % shards`, and JS `%` keeps the sign of the dividend — negative keys returned a negative shard index. The range test picks 20 random keys per run, so it failed whenever any of them hashed negative; the fixture test never caught it because every fixture key happens to hash non-negative.\n\n**Fix** (`src/shard.ts:16`): use the non-negative remainder the README and routing table specify, `((hashKey(key) % shards) + shards) % shards`.\n\n**No keys move:** for non-negative hashes the expression is identical to before, so all 20 live fixture assignments still map to the same shards; only the previously-invalid negative results change, and they land on the Python-`%` value the contract already required (`session:1:919` → 13 of 16, 1 of 10).\n\nVerified: suite run 5× consecutively, `# fail 0` each time; tests and fixtures untouched (`git diff` touches only `src/shard.ts`). `saga gate check` reports G1, G2, G3 MET / ALL MET.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:d6d8522b6d72ea1cf14cfeab204f2deb048575ed68aeadfeafb506c383c208b0","hook_ms":3,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":40605474959,"prev":"sha256:2b60d6b4a17e42a1c9787ce657d5d5b5921e202dcc38bf08f1761b304ddee004","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":20,"session":"3361d6f0-d21c-4e2c-a923-4c52ad574354","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T06:39:10.608Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
